@startuml article-lifecycle
title Presserl – Article Lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans-Serif
hide empty description

[*] --> Draft : new article

Draft --> Published : publish\n[approval chain empty]
Draft --> Submitted : submit\n[an approval level applies]
Submitted --> Submitted : approve\n[a higher level remains]
Submitted --> Published : approve\n[no level remains]
Submitted --> Draft : reject with note
Submitted --> Draft : withdraw (author)
Draft --> [*] : delete (author)
Submitted --> [*] : delete (author)

Published --> Offline : take offline\n(author, section editor,\neditor-in-chief, publisher)
Published --> Locked : emergency brake\n(publisher)
Offline --> Published : publish [chain empty]\nor approve [no level remains]
Locked --> Offline : release\n(publisher only)

Submitted : never published, waits for one level:
Submitted : section editor → editor-in-chief → publisher
Submitted : content frozen while waiting
Published : Edits create a new revision; submitting
Published : them keeps the status and the live revision
Published : until the chain approves (pending level).
Offline : Back online is submitted like changes;
Offline : the status stays Offline while it waits.
Locked : offline, only a publisher
Locked : can release it

note right of Draft
  Simplest case (first account, all roles):
  Draft → Published → Offline
  One click, no approval.
end note
@enduml
